        "signatureHash": "e312a1cd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:1c3e5d59",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Diagnostics (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:449",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Diagnostics",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 449,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "```\ngraphflow_diagnose(configPath?)\n```\n- Check provider health\n- Verify model routing\n- Debug configuration issues\n- Also returns graph stats and token savings\n\n---",
        "signatureHash": "f5d18a53"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:f1dae51b",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Workflow 8: Large-output observations & efficiency mechanisms (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:460",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Workflow 8: Large-output observations & efficiency mechanisms",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 460,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "Every efficiency mechanism is **ON by default** — the default is the best\nconfiguration (`efficiencyPolicy` in `graphflow.config.json`; switch any of\nthem off from the **GraphFlow: Settings** page or with an explicit `false`).\nSwitching one off never gates an explicit call: passing `content`/`handle`,\n`reduce:true`, or reading a returned `executionDescriptor` is explicit intent\nand always works.",
        "signatureHash": "b85bed96"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:21d03990",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Observation handles (ObservationPack) (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:469",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Observation handles (ObservationPack)",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 469,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "Archive a large tool output or log instead of replaying it in every later request:\n\n```\nStep 1: graphflow_context({ content: \"<full output>\", rootDir })\n        → { handle: \"gfo:…\", head, tail, sizeBytes, lines }\nStep 2: Keep the handle + head/tail excerpt in context; drop the full body.\nStep 3: Recall exact bytes when needed:\n        graphflow_context({ handle: \"gfo:…\", page: 0 })              # 200 lines/page\n        graphflow_context({ handle: \"gfo:…\", range: [start, end] })   # inclusive 1-based\nStep 4: Reduce a long diagnostic log to a verified receipt:\n        graphflow_context({ handle: \"gfo:…\", reduce: true, maxReceiptTokens: 400 })\n```\n\nThe receipt's retained lines are each re-read from the archive and checked\n**verbatim**; any mismatch returns a bounded excerpt (`fallback: true`) instead\nof the receipt. `efficiencyPolicy.observations` controls the inline threshold,\nhead/tail sizes, TTL, redaction, and whether reduction is local (`fingerprint`)\nor an explicit remote model (`strategy: \"llm\"` requires `provider` + `model`;\nwithout them the resolver stays local and a strategy-`llm` reduce fails open).",
        "signatureHash": "e79708b3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:9c0edf65",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Observed-pressure budget & compaction signal (Online Context Compact) (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:491",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Observed-pressure budget & compaction signal (Online Context Compact)",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 491,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "```\ngraphflow_context({\n  query: \"<question>\",\n  contextPressure: { usedTokens: 120000, maxTokens: 200000, remainingTurnsEstimate: 8 }\n})\n```\n\nOnline Context Compact is enabled by default: GraphFlow packs against a\nbudget scaled by the observed pressure (`maxContextTokens: \"auto\"`) and returns a\n`contextPressure` block with `effectiveMaxContextTokens` and, when\n`remainingTurnsEstimate` is supplied, an economic `compaction` recommendation\n(set `efficiencyPolicy.contextPressure.enabled: false` to disable).\nOmit `contextPressure` when unknown — GraphFlow never fabricates it.",
        "signatureHash": "26653e88"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:a319e510",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Fused action steps (Action Fusion) (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:507",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Fused action steps (Action Fusion)",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 507,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "Action Fusion is enabled by default: `graphflow_run`'s\n`executionDescriptor` carries `steps` (`fused: true`) where an edit and its\nimmediately following validation command collapse into one action. Execute the\nedit and its `command` in a single tool call to save one model round trip\n(set `efficiencyPolicy.actionFusion.enabled: false` to disable).\n\nThese are the defaults — every mechanism ships ON; override any field in\n`graphflow.config.json` (or toggle per mechanism in **GraphFlow: Settings**):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"efficiencyPolicy\": {\n    \"observations\": { \"enabled\": true, \"inlineThresholdBytes\": 8192 },\n    \"contextPressure\": { \"enabled\": true, \"maxContextTokens\": \"auto\", \"cacheWriteReadRatio\": 12.5 },\n    \"actionFusion\": { \"enabled\": true }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---",
        "signatureHash": "fa8f38cb"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:db23a319",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Tool Selection Decision Tree (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:530",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Tool Selection Decision Tree",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 530,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "```\nStart\n  │\n  ├─ Is this a codebase question/exploration?\n  │   └─ YES → graphflow_context ← START HERE\n  │        │\n  │        └─ Need more detail on specific item?\n  │             └─ YES → graphflow_context(anchorId)\n  │\n  ├─ Is this a multi-step coding task?\n  │   ├─ Simple (2-3 files) → context + implement\n  │   ├─ Complex → context → graphflow_plan → implement\n  │   └─ Ambiguous/high-stakes → context → graphflow_plan(mode=\"insight\") → implement\n  │\n  ├─ Do you need a complete packaged task?\n  │   └─ YES → graphflow_run (bridge mode) → execute → report_outcome\n  │\n  ├─ Did you just make file changes?\n  │   ├─ Single file → graphflow_index(filePath)\n  │   └─ Multiple files → graphflow_index (incremental)\n  │\n  ├─ Is the graph giving bad results?\n  │   ├─ First → graphflow_diagnose (check state)\n  │   ├─ Then → graphflow_index (try incremental)\n  │   └─ Last resort → graphflow_index(mode=\"full\") (full rebuild)\n  │\n  ├─ Sharing with teammates?\n  │   ├─ Export → graphflow_artifact(mode=\"export\")\n  │   └─ Import → graphflow_artifact(mode=\"import\")\n  │\n  ├─ Do you want to leverage prior learning?\n  │   └─ YES → graphflow_skill_insights\n  │\n  ├─ Tracking ROI?\n  │   └─ graphflow_diagnose (check stats field)\n  │\n  └─ Is routing/models misbehaving?\n      └─ YES → graphflow_diagnose\n```\n\n---",
        "signatureHash": "978f2d7c"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:39d66ed7",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Reading Compressed Context (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:576",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Reading Compressed Context",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 576,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "The `summary` array contains compressed context lines. Each line is one of:\n\n| Prefix | Meaning | Example |\n|--------|---------|---------|\n| `Module:` | Module-level summary | `Module: src/graph/context-slicer` |\n| `File:` | File-level summary | `File: src/graph/context-slicer.ts # exports: buildLayeredContextPackage` |\n| `Symbol:` | Function/class symbol | `Symbol: function buildLayeredContextPackage (exported) @src/graph/context-slicer.ts:42` |\n\n**Priority order:** Symbols (L1) > Files (L1) > Modules (L2) > Overview (L3)",
        "signatureHash": "4bebc71"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:1fbb815f",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Token Budget (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:588",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Token Budget",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 588,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "Always pay attention to `tokenBudget`:\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `maxContextTokens` | The configured budget (default 1500) |\n| `estimatedRawTokens` | What reading all relevant files raw would cost (floored at the actual delivered size — never reported below it) |\n| `compressedTokens` | What GraphFlow's compressed output uses |\n| `estimatedSavingsPercent` | Percentage saved, computed on `accountedTokens` (typically 70-95%) |\n| `budgetUsedPercent` | How much of the budget is used |\n| `unbudgetedTokens` | Out-of-package payloads the response also carries (dialogue recall hits, workbench/dialogue preview echoes) — counted outside `tokenBudget`, never hidden |\n| `accountedTokens` | `compressedTokens` + `unbudgetedTokens`: the true delivered total the savings % is computed on |\n| `contextPressure` | Present only when observed-pressure budgeting is enabled: `effectiveMaxContextTokens` plus an optional `compaction` signal |\n\n**Rule of thumb:** If `budgetUsedPercent < 50%`, you can safely expand more anchors. When reporting savings, quote `accountedTokens` too — savings % alone understates the real payload you received.\n\n---",
        "signatureHash": "7d09f910"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:34bbf9f2",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: 1. Context First, Always (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:609",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: 1. Context First, Always",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 609,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "- Start EVERY coding task with `graphflow_context`\n- Only read full files when compressed context is insufficient\n- Never grep the whole repo before trying GraphFlow",
        "signatureHash": "f3fc8fba"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:96bf4b7c",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: 2. Plan Before Complex Work (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:614",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: 2. Plan Before Complex Work",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 614,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "- Use `graphflow_plan` for anything beyond 2-3 files\n- Use `graphflow_plan(mode=\"insight\")` for ambiguous tasks\n- Follow the DAG order (respect dependencies)\n- Use context from GraphFlow at each step",
        "signatureHash": "77c4aab1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:43f76993",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: 3. Keep Graph Fresh (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:620",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: 3. Keep Graph Fresh",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 620,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "- Call `graphflow_index(filePath)` after saving individual files\n- Call `graphflow_index` after significant changes\n- Prefer incremental index over full rebuild\n- Check `graphflow_diagnose` if results seem off",
        "signatureHash": "16c1c8a5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:839c359c",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: 4. Close the Learning Loop (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:626",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: 4. Close the Learning Loop",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 626,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "- After bridge-mode runs, call `graphflow_report_outcome`\n- Include lessons learned to improve future planning\n- This feeds the skill evolution flywheel",
        "signatureHash": "dd1f2b3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:3459c975",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: 5. Report Token Savings (honest accounting) (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:631",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: 5. Report Token Savings (honest accounting)",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 631,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "- Report `accountedTokens` = `compressedTokens` + `unbudgetedTokens`, together with `estimatedSavingsPercent`\n- Savings % is computed on the accounted total (it includes out-of-package payloads like dialogue hits and preview echoes); quoting only savings % understates the true delivered payload\n- Include raw (`estimatedRawTokens`) vs accounted token counts",
        "signatureHash": "2914fe40"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:42b44115",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: 6. Bridge Mode Mindset (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:636",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: 6. Bridge Mode Mindset",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 636,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "- `graphflow_run` returns plans, it doesn't execute them\n- YOU are the execution agent (bridge mode)\n- Use the packaged context to accelerate your work\n\n---",
        "signatureHash": "8f38c54a"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:77f2a7e5",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: \"0 anchors found\" or empty results (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:645",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: \"0 anchors found\" or empty results",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 645,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
        "signature": "1. **Chinese/CJK:** translate to English keywords; pass `englishQuery` or answer `agentWorkItems` id `query-translate-en`\n2. Check if graph exists: `graphflow_diagnose`\n3. If empty: run `graphflow_index`\n4. If still empty: verify `rootDir` points to correct project",
        "signatureHash": "e3aab9d3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:4238b890",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Results seem stale (exported) @.graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md:651",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Results seem stale",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 651,
        "file": ".graphflow/skills/graphflow/SKILL.md",
