    {
      "id": "symbol:.github/copilot-instructions.md:77ff179b",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: GraphFlow Token-First Rule (GitHub Copilot) (exported) @.github/copilot-instructions.md:1",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: GraphFlow Token-First Rule (GitHub Copilot)",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 1,
        "file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md",
        "signature": "<!-- GRAPHFLOW:BEGIN managed block — edit outside these markers only -->\n# GraphFlow Token-First Rule (GitHub Copilot)\n\nGraphFlow is a graph-based context and planning service backed by a persistent MCP server. It turns codebases into queryable knowledge graphs, delivering token-efficient compressed context, task planning, and orchestration.\n\nBefore broad code exploration, implementation, debugging, review, planning, or architecture questions:\n\n1. Call `graphflow_context` with the user's task/query.\n2. Use the returned `summary`, `anchors`, `refillPreview`, and `tokenBudget` as the first context source.\n3. Read full files only when:\n   - GraphFlow anchors point to that file/symbol,\n   - the compressed context is insufficient,\n   - or exact edits require the file body.\n4. For multi-step or ambiguous work, call `graphflow_plan` before implementation.\n5. For graph freshness after project changes, call `graphflow_index`.\n6. Report token budget when available:\n   - estimated raw tokens,\n   - compressed tokens,\n   - estimated savings percent,\n   - max context token budget.\n\nDo not scan the whole repository, recursively inspect many files, or read large files before trying GraphFlow context.",
        "signatureHash": "9eeb4864"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.github/copilot-instructions.md:eea46dbc",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Workspace root (`rootDir`) (exported) @.github/copilot-instructions.md:25",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Workspace root (`rootDir`)",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 25,
        "file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md",
        "signature": "Pass `rootDir` = the absolute path of the project you are working in. **Never** pass your home directory, AppData, or an unexpanded `${workspaceFolder}` placeholder — GraphFlow refuses unsafe workspace roots and the call fails. If a tool answers `unsafe workspace root`, retry the same call without `rootDir` (the server then uses its configured workspace) or with the project path.",
        "signatureHash": "5d38ea50"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.github/copilot-instructions.md:6bbdb86f",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: VS Code / Copilot MCP setup (exported) @.github/copilot-instructions.md:29",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: VS Code / Copilot MCP setup",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 29,
        "file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md",
        "signature": "Ensure GraphFlow MCP is configured in `~/.config/Code/User/mcp.json` (Linux) or project `.vscode/mcp.json` under the `servers` key:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"servers\": {\n    \"graphflow\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"--package=@roarpeng/graphflow\", \"graphflow-mcp\"],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"GRAPHFLOW_MCP_STDIO\": \"1\",\n        \"GRAPHFLOW_LOG_JSON\": \"1\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDo **not** hardcode `GRAPHFLOW_WORKSPACE_ROOT` — let the MCP server detect the open workspace.",
        "signatureHash": "fbb66f0f"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.github/copilot-instructions.md:59afe47c",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Chinese / CJK queries (agent must translate) (exported) @.github/copilot-instructions.md:50",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Chinese / CJK queries (agent must translate)",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 50,
        "file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md",
        "signature": "Code symbols are mostly English. For Chinese user questions:\n\n1. **Proactive:** Before or with `graphflow_context`, translate intent to English **file/class/component names** (e.g. `PoseDetectionPage`, `BattlePage`, `shieldEffect`) and pass `englishQuery`. Avoid generic terms like `exercise` when the user means UI/camera — they often match data/types layers.\n2. **Module families (store/slices):** Prefer file stems (`useGameStore companionSlice dailySlice inventorySlice`), not bare domain words like `monster` (often hits `data/monsters` instead of `monsterSlice`).\n3. **Reactive:** If preview returns `agentWorkItems` with `query-translate-en` (low `anchorCount`), answer the JSON prompt with your model, then retry preview with `englishQuery`.\n4. Keep `query` as the original Chinese text; use `englishQuery` for search terms only.",
        "signatureHash": "1f3e1226"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.github/copilot-instructions.md:dbcceeb9",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: High-frequency MCP tools (exported) @.github/copilot-instructions.md:59",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: High-frequency MCP tools",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 59,
        "file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md",
        "signature": "| Tool | When |\n|------|------|\n| `graphflow_context` | **Always first** for code questions (use `query`); expand anchor with `anchorId` |\n| `graphflow_plan` | Multi-step tasks |\n| `graphflow_run` | Full task packaging (bridge mode) |\n| `graphflow_report_outcome` | After executing a `graphflow_run` descriptor |\n| `graphflow_index` | After significant edits |",
        "signatureHash": "d48f109b"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "symbol:.github/copilot-instructions.md:370b62d4",
      "type": "Symbol",
      "content": "chunk chunk: Bridge-mode outcome reporting (exported) @.github/copilot-instructions.md:69",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "chunk: Bridge-mode outcome reporting",
        "kind": "chunk",
        "exported": true,
        "line": 69,
        "file": ".github/copilot-instructions.md",
        "signature": "After `graphflow_run`, **must** call `graphflow_report_outcome` with `episodeId`, `success`, and optional `lessons`.\n\nCLI fallback when MCP is unavailable:\n\n```bash\ngraphflow --json context preview \"<query>\"\ngraphflow --json plan \"<task>\"\ngraphflow --json outcome report <episodeId> <success>\n```\n\nTreat GraphFlow outputs as structured machine-readable data, not prose.\n<!-- GRAPHFLOW:END -->",
        "signatureHash": "ecdbf6b9"
      }
    },
